From: Gil Noh <nohtaegil@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Unregister an msync wait when the contention check returns early.

msync_wait_multiple() sends its register message to wineserver and then
spins on check_shm_contention(). When that sees an object already
signaled it returns STATUS_PENDING without calling server_remove_wait(),
unlike every other exit path. The server still processes the queued
registration and adds the thread to the wait list of each object it finds
unsignaled. Those nodes are freed only by a later server-side signal of
the same object, so for an object that is never signaled -- typically a
worker thread's quit event in WaitForMultipleObjects({quit, work}) -- one
node leaks per early return.

The node pool in server/msync.c holds 0x80000 entries. A long session of
Fantasy General II (Unity 2018.4) took the early return millions of times,
exhausted the pool ("msync: warn: node memory pool exhausted" on every
allocation) and saturated every core.

Reproduced with a two-thread WaitForMultipleObjects({quit, work})
ping-pong, 200,000 round trips, with wineserver node accounting:

                         in_use nodes      longest list   regs - unregs
  without this patch     4,051, rising     4,002          4,017
  with this patch        ~50, flat         5              17 (live waits)

The leaked-node count, registrations without an unregister and early
returns agree. With the patch, a long Fantasy General II session showed
7.18 M early returns and 32.8 M registrations with in_use flat at ~230.

server_remove_wait() also drops multiple_waiters, including on the alert
object, which the open-coded loop it replaces did not.

Known cost, cause not yet understood: on the microbenchmark above the
patched build is slower per round trip (8.1 us -> 13.1 us mean over five
interleaved pairs) and makes about twice as many server registrations for
the same work. Not noticeable in the game.

Against CrossOver 26.3.0 sources (Wine 11.0). LGPL-2.1-or-later.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
index ae46bf3..bfa5685 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/msync.c
@@ -377,15 +377,14 @@ static NTSTATUS msync_wait_multiple( const int *objs, void **objs_shm, int alert
     {
         if (check_shm_contention( objs_shm, alert_obj_shm, count, tid ))
         {
-            int i;
-            for (i = 0; i < count; i++)
-            {
-                struct event *obj = (struct event *)objs_shm[i];
-
-                int refs = __atomic_sub_fetch( &obj->multiple_waiters, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
-                if (refs < 0)
-                    __atomic_store_n( &obj->multiple_waiters, 0, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
-            }
+            /* The register message is already queued, and the server will add
+             * this thread to the wait lists of every object it finds unsignaled.
+             * Unregister, as every other exit path does: otherwise those nodes
+             * stay on the lists until the object is next signaled through the
+             * server, which for an event that never fires is never, and the
+             * server's node pool is eventually exhausted. server_remove_wait
+             * also drops multiple_waiters, including on the alert object. */
+            server_remove_wait( msgh_id, objs, objs_shm, alert_obj, alert_obj_shm, count );
             return STATUS_PENDING;
         }
     }
